        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): stop retrying non-idempotent sends on post-connect-ambiguous errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nDiscord message creates can complete at Discord while the client receives a transport failure. Retrying the same non-idempotent create without a server deduplication key can deliver a duplicate message.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEach affected Discord create now receives a 24-character random nonce with `enforce_nonce: true`. The nonce is built once before the retry runner, so a retry returns the existing message rather than creating another. This covers text, media, components, forum/media thread starter messages, approvals, and voice messages.\n\nThe non-idempotent retry classifier keeps pre-connect failures and rate limits retryable, and now also keeps HTTP 502 retryable. Discord documents 502 as a gateway-unavailable response that clients should retry; nonce enforcement makes that retry safe for supported message create bodies.\n\n## Why this is the right boundary\n\nThe retry module still owns retry classification. Message construction owns the create nonce, which remains stable for all attempts of one logical create. Idempotent REST operations retain the broad transient retry policy unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/discord/src/retry.test.ts extensions/discord/src/send.message-request.test.ts extensions/discord/src/outbound-payload.contract.test.ts extensions/discord/src/client.test.ts extensions/discord/src/outbound-adapter.test.ts` passed before the final rebase; the same focused suite was queued behind another active local package-artifact check after rebasing.\n- Scoped `tsgo` passed for production and core test projects before the final rebase.\n- Scoped `oxlint` and `oxfmt --check` passed before the final rebase.\n- Structured closeout review completed with no actionable findings.\n\n## Real behavior proof\nBehavior addressed: a gateway-unavailable response after a message create previously replayed the create and delivered a duplicate.\nReal environment tested: the production Discord `RequestClient`, `createChannelMessage`, request serialization, retry runner, and a real localhost TCP HTTP connection on pristine main 5a48e73973 and this patch; the controlled server records the create before returning HTTP 502, then applies the same nonce-enforcement contract as Discord on the retry.\nExact steps or command run after this patch: `tsx --tsconfig tsconfig.json /tmp/discord-network-fault-proof.ts /root/openclaw-pr-discord-retry patched`, with the identical command against `/root/openclaw` for pristine main.\nEvidence after fix:\n```\n# BEFORE (pristine main 5a48e73973)\nserverSideMessagesCreated=2 | send RESOLVED id=discord-msg-2 | requests=2\n\n# AFTER (this patch, identical HTTP 502 sequence)\nserverSideMessagesCreated=1 | send RESOLVED id=discord-msg-1 | requests=2\n```\nObserved result after fix: the first request is retried after the gateway-unavailable response, and the repeated nonce returns the original message so exactly one message is created.\nWhat was not tested: no request was sent to Discord production; the controlled network fault uses a local HTTP server and does not exercise Discord credentials, permissions, or rate limits.\n",
